1
00:00:05,801 --> 00:00:07,281
(All characters, places, and organizations
in this drama are fictitious.)

2
00:00:07,306 --> 00:00:08,814
(Filming followed broadcast guidelines
for minors, some scenes used AI.)

3
00:00:09,417 --> 00:00:11,112
Don't touch her.

4
00:00:12,088 --> 00:00:14,094
Don't you touch my mom!

5
00:00:15,067 --> 00:00:17,343
Who are you to lay a hand on my mom?

6
00:00:18,161 --> 00:00:21,001
I said don't touch my mom!

7
00:00:33,714 --> 00:00:35,898
Mom? What mom?

8
00:00:36,027 --> 00:00:38,170
She married a rich man to live in luxury,

9
00:00:38,195 --> 00:00:41,531
and abandoned you poor kids
for 17 years, didn't she?

10
00:00:41,852 --> 00:00:45,594
How can you call someone like that Mom?

11
00:00:49,134 --> 00:00:50,398
Gyu Rim.

12
00:00:55,460 --> 00:00:57,822
Whose collar do you think you're grabbing?

13
00:00:58,214 --> 00:01:00,431
I'm your stepmom.

14
00:01:00,768 --> 00:01:04,713
I fed you, clothed you, and raised you
for over two years,

15
00:01:04,738 --> 00:01:06,147
and you dare treat me like this?

16
00:01:06,172 --> 00:01:09,758
Back then, I was weak and stupid,
so I kept quiet,

17
00:01:11,324 --> 00:01:17,067
but I'm all grown up now,
and I know right from wrong,

18
00:01:17,574 --> 00:01:22,010
and I'm not the Han Gyu Rim
you used to push around, lady.

19
00:01:25,494 --> 00:01:27,901
Yeah. Okay. I get it.

20
00:01:28,114 --> 00:01:31,602
I get it, so let go of this first.

21
00:01:31,680 --> 00:01:34,260
If you ever hurt my mom again,
even the tiniest bit,

22
00:01:35,294 --> 00:01:36,672
I won't let you get away with it.

23
00:01:37,800 --> 00:01:42,217
I'll crush someone like you
with my own two hands.

24
00:01:42,667 --> 00:01:45,807
I'll grind you to dust. Got it?

25
00:01:47,334 --> 00:01:53,918
Yes. I get it. So let go of me.

26
00:01:54,433 --> 00:01:58,261
Are you really trying to kill me?

27
00:02:01,622 --> 00:02:03,754
I can't handle shock.

28
00:02:04,427 --> 00:02:06,442
I have a bad heart,

29
00:02:06,495 --> 00:02:12,235
and I even had heart surgery
three years ago.

30
00:02:22,154 --> 00:02:23,821
Mom, you get up too.

31
00:02:27,720 --> 00:02:30,359
Why would you kneel before me?

32
00:02:38,254 --> 00:02:41,744
What did you do that was so wrong?

33
00:02:43,427 --> 00:02:46,246
You must've had it the hardest.

34
00:02:46,681 --> 00:02:49,233
You're the biggest victim here!

35
00:02:51,107 --> 00:02:53,893
I'm sorry, Gyu Rim.

36
00:02:55,727 --> 00:03:01,389
I've wronged you so terribly.

37
00:03:03,494 --> 00:03:07,052
I'm sorry, Gyu Rim.

38
00:03:07,077 --> 00:03:11,540
I'm so sorry.

39
00:03:16,074 --> 00:03:18,749
What a scene. Somebody roll the cameras!

40
00:03:38,254 --> 00:03:40,736
Get up, Mom. Please.

41
00:03:41,459 --> 00:03:43,807
Things like that can happen in life.

42
00:03:45,414 --> 00:03:48,949
Sometimes life doesn't go your way.

43
00:03:50,580 --> 00:03:53,681
Maybe you had your reasons.

44
00:03:54,765 --> 00:03:57,159
I said get up. Please.

45
00:04:00,100 --> 00:04:03,516
Gyu Rim, I'm sorry.

46
00:04:12,589 --> 00:04:14,861
(Episode 32)

47
00:04:15,161 --> 00:04:17,884
- Is this special treatment too?
- Totally.

48
00:04:17,948 --> 00:04:20,195
- Not even the president gets this.
- Not even the president gets this.

49
00:04:22,654 --> 00:04:24,934
Enjoy your meal, VVIP guest.

50
00:04:25,041 --> 00:04:28,102
Thank you. This looks great.

51
00:04:36,707 --> 00:04:39,518
What's wrong? Not good?

52
00:04:44,901 --> 00:04:46,516
You've got something to tell me, right?

53
00:04:48,674 --> 00:04:50,782
It's a secret from Mom for now.

54
00:04:51,807 --> 00:04:53,826
I met your mom.

55
00:04:58,421 --> 00:05:00,274
- My mom?
- Yes.

56
00:05:02,071 --> 00:05:05,954
- When?
- Earlier. At the spicy rice cake place.

57
00:05:10,234 --> 00:05:11,649
That must've caught you off guard.

58
00:05:11,767 --> 00:05:14,806
It's okay. I've met her once before.

59
00:05:22,341 --> 00:05:26,038
So what did you two talk about?

60
00:05:26,300 --> 00:05:29,938
- That I'm not a burden, I'm a blessing.
- What?

61
00:05:30,687 --> 00:05:34,287
Your mom said I'm not a burden,
I'm a blessing.

62
00:05:35,372 --> 00:05:36,521
Really?

63
00:05:38,068 --> 00:05:40,915
My mom said that when adults praise me,

64
00:05:41,147 --> 00:05:47,269
I should say, "Thanks for the kind words,"
and be modest about it,

65
00:05:48,273 --> 00:05:52,202
but honestly, I think your mom
is kind of right.

66
00:05:52,654 --> 00:05:56,924
I'm good at studying, sports, and drawing.

67
00:05:56,949 --> 00:06:00,941
There's really nothing I can't do.
Not to brag, though.

68
00:06:01,014 --> 00:06:04,151
No, I know.

69
00:06:04,374 --> 00:06:09,132
Whenever Da Som's mom sees my mom,
she says she's so jealous...

70
00:06:09,157 --> 00:06:10,879
that my mom has a smart son like me.

71
00:06:11,420 --> 00:06:12,839
Not to brag, though.

72
00:06:12,864 --> 00:06:15,756
No, that's a fact.

73
00:06:16,067 --> 00:06:21,601
So I'm not a burden. I'm a blessing,
just like your mom said, right?

74
00:06:21,626 --> 00:06:25,316
Of course. Hey, who called you a burden?

75
00:06:25,347 --> 00:06:26,983
Bring them to me. I'll...

76
00:06:27,777 --> 00:06:31,143
knead them into dough!

77
00:06:32,933 --> 00:06:37,814
But why are your eyes getting red?

78
00:06:38,620 --> 00:06:40,923
Mine? No, they're not.

79
00:06:42,586 --> 00:06:44,068
I must've gotten something in my eye.

80
00:06:45,250 --> 00:06:51,408
Anyway, Mom, you, your mom,

81
00:06:51,788 --> 00:06:56,655
and my family are all going to be
prouder and prouder of me.

82
00:06:57,421 --> 00:06:59,289
That's all you need to know.

83
00:07:00,334 --> 00:07:03,426
I'll keep that in mind. Eat up.

84
00:07:06,508 --> 00:07:08,589
This is seriously good.

85
00:07:12,760 --> 00:07:16,694
Gyeol, you've got this.

86
00:07:51,934 --> 00:07:53,446
Hello, is this Mr. Lee Hyeon Beom?

87
00:07:55,033 --> 00:07:56,507
This is Kim Mu Jin.

88
00:07:58,067 --> 00:08:01,654
If you have time this evening,
could we meet briefly?

89
00:08:02,377 --> 00:08:04,483
There's something I need to tell you.

90
00:08:07,306 --> 00:08:10,063
Yes. It's about Gyeol.

91
00:08:20,174 --> 00:08:23,444
I never imagined she'd be
the twins' birth mother.

92
00:08:32,374 --> 00:08:33,793
Thank you.

93
00:08:40,400 --> 00:08:42,454
You add vinegar and mustard, right?

94
00:08:52,388 --> 00:08:58,507
Right. You used to put a lot of vinegar
in your cold noodles, I think.

95
00:09:00,166 --> 00:09:01,678
Do I remember that right?

96
00:09:04,534 --> 00:09:05,800
You do.

97
00:09:16,054 --> 00:09:17,167
Go ahead.

98
00:09:19,820 --> 00:09:21,754
I'm not big on vinegar,

99
00:09:22,081 --> 00:09:26,881
but my Gyeol loves vinegar
in his cold noodles. That little guy.

100
00:09:32,821 --> 00:09:34,998
I have an eight-year-old son.

101
00:09:41,200 --> 00:09:43,744
Seo Hyeon told me...

102
00:09:45,358 --> 00:09:47,571
that the baby didn't make it...

103
00:09:51,154 --> 00:09:55,826
When my baby left,
it sent me another little one.

104
00:10:06,554 --> 00:10:11,964
I know I have no right to ask this...

105
00:10:15,000 --> 00:10:16,794
What do you mean?

106
00:10:18,387 --> 00:10:21,648
He was born from my heart.

107
00:10:23,148 --> 00:10:28,123
You have no idea how sweet, kind,
smart, and devoted my Gyeol is.

108
00:10:29,061 --> 00:10:31,590
You'll probably fall for him
the moment you see him, Mom.

109
00:10:33,384 --> 00:10:35,810
Your noodles will get soggy. Eat up.

110
00:10:37,960 --> 00:10:39,642
Should we order some dumplings too?

111
00:10:46,025 --> 00:10:48,865
(Damga Charcoal Grill)

112
00:10:57,247 --> 00:11:00,855
What did you do that was so wrong?

113
00:11:01,287 --> 00:11:04,048
You must've had it the hardest.

114
00:11:05,368 --> 00:11:07,928
You're the biggest victim here!

115
00:11:08,328 --> 00:11:10,361
Get up, Mom. Please.

116
00:11:10,647 --> 00:11:13,085
Things like that can happen in life.

117
00:11:13,214 --> 00:11:16,533
Sometimes life doesn't go your way.

118
00:11:17,132 --> 00:11:20,196
Maybe you had your reasons.

119
00:11:21,505 --> 00:11:23,664
I said get up. Please.

120
00:11:26,627 --> 00:11:29,913
How can you forgive me so easily?

121
00:11:32,654 --> 00:11:37,789
How can my daughter be such a pushover?

122
00:12:48,322 --> 00:12:49,460
Are you okay?

123
00:12:51,947 --> 00:12:55,179
Thank you. For the handkerchief.

124
00:12:56,894 --> 00:13:00,432
It's windy this time of year,
so keep dust out of your eyes.

125
00:13:01,515 --> 00:13:02,878
What should I eat today?

126
00:13:05,240 --> 00:13:06,780
Let's see.

127
00:13:11,514 --> 00:13:16,197
I must've saved the country
in a past life.

128
00:13:18,134 --> 00:13:21,093
I should be punished,
but I keep getting rewarded.

129
00:13:21,574 --> 00:13:24,413
Why would you be punished?
You deserve a reward.

130
00:13:25,154 --> 00:13:27,536
Should I list all the reasons
you deserve one?

131
00:13:27,614 --> 00:13:29,127
I could go on all day.

132
00:13:30,514 --> 00:13:32,077
What's good today?

133
00:13:35,547 --> 00:13:38,636
Dad, you're here too?

134
00:13:38,880 --> 00:13:40,851
- Seo Hyeon.
- Seo Hyeon.

135
00:13:44,053 --> 00:13:47,004
Seo Hyeon, I have something to talk about
with your mom today,

136
00:13:47,211 --> 00:13:49,437
so unless it's important,
maybe next time...

137
00:13:49,494 --> 00:13:51,085
I have something to talk about too.

138
00:13:52,161 --> 00:13:53,946
Mom needs to know some things.

139
00:13:59,773 --> 00:14:01,556
Why? What is it?

140
00:14:02,041 --> 00:14:06,220
Mom, is Han Gyu Yeong
really your biological daughter?

141
00:14:09,267 --> 00:14:10,908
She looks nothing like you.

142
00:14:11,007 --> 00:14:12,858
Is she even Han Gyu Rim's real sister?

143
00:14:12,883 --> 00:14:14,023
Seo Hyeon, that's enough.

144
00:14:15,320 --> 00:14:17,010
What happened?

145
00:14:17,035 --> 00:14:21,718
Han Gyu Rim is as sweet as they come,
but Han Gyu Yeong is pure evil...

146
00:14:21,743 --> 00:14:24,451
Jang Seo Hyeon, stop it.

147
00:14:28,987 --> 00:14:31,976
She's seriously so weird.

148
00:14:32,143 --> 00:14:33,937
She says she'll get revenge on Dad.

149
00:14:34,141 --> 00:14:37,004
She ruined her own life,
so why is she threatening you?

150
00:14:37,441 --> 00:14:41,105
And you're going along with it
like she's got dirt on you.

151
00:14:41,840 --> 00:14:44,880
What are you talking about? Let's go.

152
00:14:46,120 --> 00:14:48,812
Did you drive here? I'll get you a cab.
Let's go, hurry.

153
00:14:48,868 --> 00:14:51,754
If you give me the green light,
I'll beat her to a pulp.

154
00:14:51,847 --> 00:14:54,348
Come on, let's go. Get up.

155
00:14:54,393 --> 00:14:56,169
Honey, wait.

156
00:14:57,718 --> 00:14:59,651
It's okay, Seo Hyeon. Tell me.

157
00:15:00,761 --> 00:15:02,941
Why? What about Gyu Yeong?

158
00:15:03,641 --> 00:15:05,669
What did Gyu Yeong do this time?

159
00:15:18,214 --> 00:15:20,559
Well, the thing is...

160
00:15:23,808 --> 00:15:26,432
I don't know. I suddenly can't remember.

161
00:15:26,699 --> 00:15:28,686
It's okay. Tell me.

162
00:15:29,221 --> 00:15:31,321
I deserve to know.

163
00:15:33,241 --> 00:15:37,117
Why? What on earth is going on?

164
00:15:37,467 --> 00:15:39,516
What happened this time?

165
00:15:49,500 --> 00:15:54,339
They say a birth mother's bond runs deep.
She still took her mother's side.

166
00:15:55,307 --> 00:15:57,571
Blood is blood.

167
00:15:57,734 --> 00:16:01,850
Blood is thicker than water, right?

168
00:16:03,887 --> 00:16:06,854
Just looking at that shameless thing,

169
00:16:06,879 --> 00:16:11,389
I feel like stress will kill me first.
What do I do?

170
00:16:11,414 --> 00:16:13,937
She's still a customer, though.

171
00:16:14,027 --> 00:16:16,274
What customer? Her?

172
00:16:16,299 --> 00:16:20,509
I have my own flesh and blood too.

173
00:16:21,034 --> 00:16:24,543
I have a son and a daughter too.

174
00:16:24,568 --> 00:16:27,427
Don't give me
that flesh-and-blood nonsense.

175
00:16:28,021 --> 00:16:34,010
You heard the twins too, right?
Gyu Seo and Gyu Min?

176
00:16:35,687 --> 00:16:41,898
What did they say
whenever their mom came up?

177
00:16:42,127 --> 00:16:45,027
Why? What did they say?

178
00:16:46,555 --> 00:16:49,288
I can't bring myself to say it.

179
00:16:49,421 --> 00:16:52,183
Why? Because if you heard it,

180
00:16:52,477 --> 00:16:55,283
you'd die of shame,
so I can't tell you. So what?

181
00:16:55,308 --> 00:16:57,164
You old hag!

182
00:16:57,251 --> 00:16:58,563
Old hag?

183
00:16:58,701 --> 00:17:04,638
Fine. Want me to hit you
with the hard facts?

184
00:17:04,860 --> 00:17:11,354
Want me to lay out exactly
how your own kids really see you?

185
00:17:11,640 --> 00:17:14,412
Fine, go ahead. Spill it if you want.

186
00:17:14,437 --> 00:17:15,870
You shameless woman!

187
00:17:16,157 --> 00:17:18,190
- Gyu Min just walked into the shop.
- Gyu Rim!

188
00:17:22,380 --> 00:17:24,776
Where did she go, leaving the shop empty?

189
00:17:28,634 --> 00:17:30,599
She's coming this way!

190
00:17:33,161 --> 00:17:34,629
Hello.

191
00:17:35,072 --> 00:17:36,609
- Hi.
- Hi there.

192
00:17:38,183 --> 00:17:40,297
- I made these rice rolls.
- Okay.

193
00:17:40,654 --> 00:17:42,538
They're not very good, but try them.

194
00:17:42,563 --> 00:17:44,620
Thank you, Gyu Min.

195
00:17:44,645 --> 00:17:48,263
My goodness, you made rice rolls?

196
00:17:48,507 --> 00:17:51,091
Aren't you something.

197
00:17:51,133 --> 00:17:53,474
Yes, for the Sunday special.

198
00:17:53,874 --> 00:17:56,630
Right. By the way, do you know
where Gyu Rim went?

199
00:17:57,094 --> 00:17:58,825
There's nobody at the shop.

200
00:17:58,907 --> 00:18:00,787
Even the new lady she hired isn't there.

201
00:18:01,991 --> 00:18:05,131
Well. Where could everyone be?

202
00:18:05,214 --> 00:18:08,965
Here, sweetie, go buy yourself
some spicy rice cakes.

203
00:18:08,990 --> 00:18:11,553
- No, it's okay.
- Take it. Go on.

204
00:18:11,578 --> 00:18:13,878
Thank you.

205
00:18:14,387 --> 00:18:17,075
I'll get going, then. Goodbye.

206
00:18:17,100 --> 00:18:19,860
- Tell Gyu Rim I brought rice rolls.
- Okay.

207
00:18:20,127 --> 00:18:22,786
- I'll be going.
- Take care.

208
00:18:22,811 --> 00:18:24,519
- You too.
- Okay.

209
00:18:28,454 --> 00:18:29,922
Gyu Min's gone.

210
00:18:30,528 --> 00:18:32,859
Move. My guts are about to burst.

211
00:18:34,501 --> 00:18:36,152
My heart...

212
00:18:37,280 --> 00:18:38,825
Did you see that?

213
00:18:39,279 --> 00:18:44,685
Did you see what a fine, upstanding
young lady Gyu Min has become?

214
00:18:44,716 --> 00:18:49,844
Of course she turned out pretty.
I gave birth to her, after all.

215
00:18:52,453 --> 00:18:56,476
Your mouth may be crooked,
but at least speak straight.

216
00:18:56,674 --> 00:18:59,984
Those twins you abandoned as newborns...

217
00:19:00,009 --> 00:19:06,273
Even their dad lost his mind, left home
to find you, and abandoned them,

218
00:19:06,506 --> 00:19:12,857
so Gyu Rim changed their dirty diapers,
carried them on her back, fed them milk...

219
00:19:12,882 --> 00:19:18,036
Not just one, but two.
Four, counting her own siblings...

220
00:19:18,287 --> 00:19:23,440
She worked herself to the bone
raising them.

221
00:19:24,701 --> 00:19:26,838
Gyu Rim was just a kid herself.

222
00:19:27,561 --> 00:19:31,023
A kid who should've grown up
loved by her parents.

223
00:19:32,961 --> 00:19:39,208
If you don't appreciate what Gyu Rim did,
you'll pay for it someday, woman!

224
00:19:40,787 --> 00:19:43,807
I heard that brat Gyu Yeong
was mean to them.

225
00:19:43,838 --> 00:19:46,949
She hit my twins with a tambourine,

226
00:19:46,987 --> 00:19:52,432
wouldn't let them eat ice cream,
and bullied them like a wicked stepsister.

227
00:19:52,457 --> 00:19:55,342
Hey! You!

228
00:19:55,367 --> 00:19:57,886
Let go! Throw her out!

229
00:19:58,194 --> 00:19:59,962
Please leave, ma'am!

230
00:20:05,134 --> 00:20:10,497
You're a good girl after all.
It must've been hard pretending to be bad.

231
00:20:12,694 --> 00:20:16,941
Never in my life have I heard anyone
call me nice.

232
00:20:17,241 --> 00:20:19,588
What? Expert-level gaslighting?

233
00:20:19,701 --> 00:20:22,914
Why? What's he planning? What's his angle?

234
00:20:24,881 --> 00:20:28,779
- It's me. Can I come in?
- Yes.

235
00:20:38,381 --> 00:20:40,856
Gyu Min made rice rolls.

236
00:20:40,987 --> 00:20:45,545
The sides burst and they look a mess,
but they taste great.

237
00:20:50,180 --> 00:20:51,421
What's your angle?

238
00:20:51,560 --> 00:20:55,422
You haven't eaten all day,
so I didn't want you to starve.

239
00:20:55,461 --> 00:20:56,821
Not that.

240
00:20:56,955 --> 00:21:01,208
You told me I'm a good girl after all,
that it must've been hard acting bad.

241
00:21:01,280 --> 00:21:02,713
Why are you gaslighting me?

242
00:21:02,738 --> 00:21:04,279
I'm not gaslighting you.

243
00:21:04,514 --> 00:21:06,396
I just said what I felt.

244
00:21:06,421 --> 00:21:07,876
I'm not nice.

245
00:21:07,901 --> 00:21:10,089
You know better than anyone
how nasty I am.

246
00:21:10,114 --> 00:21:13,203
Then I guess I was wrong about you.

247
00:21:13,228 --> 00:21:14,996
I'm telling you, you weren't wrong.

248
00:21:15,021 --> 00:21:16,722
I'm the wicked stepsister.
I'm the mean girl.

249
00:21:16,747 --> 00:21:19,986
Right, you were the wicked stepsister
and the mean girl,

250
00:21:20,093 --> 00:21:23,259
but it seems you've finally grown up
and repented.

251
00:21:23,284 --> 00:21:26,693
I haven't grown up.
And I haven't repented.

252
00:21:29,874 --> 00:21:35,574
Fine. You haven't grown up or repented,
so just call yourself a bad person.

253
00:21:38,407 --> 00:21:41,919
Heung Sik, do you happen to like me?

254
00:21:43,574 --> 00:21:47,358
Have you lost your mind?
Are you on something?

255
00:21:48,527 --> 00:21:52,147
No, there's definitely an angle here.

256
00:21:53,321 --> 00:21:56,669
You're a pro, aren't you? You've played
lots of women this way, haven't you?

257
00:21:56,694 --> 00:21:58,792
What, running low on cash lately?

258
00:22:01,795 --> 00:22:06,501
Delude yourself all you want,
but don't take it too far.

259
00:22:06,901 --> 00:22:09,399
Even when I compliment you, you freak out.

260
00:22:14,740 --> 00:22:18,485
You're the first person in my life
to ever call me nice.

261
00:22:18,510 --> 00:22:20,902
Why would you say that?
What's your angle, seriously?

262
00:22:20,927 --> 00:22:22,735
Angle, my foot.

263
00:22:23,887 --> 00:22:26,831
I looked beyond your appearance
and saw who you really are. So what?

264
00:22:26,856 --> 00:22:31,170
You're afraid someone will notice
the soft, squishy roe inside you,

265
00:22:31,261 --> 00:22:33,127
so you bristle up,

266
00:22:33,152 --> 00:22:36,543
and lash out like an angry sea urchin.
That's why. Happy?

267
00:22:38,694 --> 00:22:40,316
Sea urchin, my foot.

268
00:22:40,341 --> 00:22:42,273
Do you know how much I hate sea urchins?

269
00:22:42,298 --> 00:22:45,630
Anyway, try gaslighting me one more time
by calling me nice or whatever.

270
00:22:45,655 --> 00:22:47,696
I'll tell Park Su Nam
about your double life,

271
00:22:47,721 --> 00:22:51,704
how you pretend to be jobless
while working as a photographer!

272
00:22:54,187 --> 00:22:59,542
Never in my life have I seen someone
get mad over a compliment.

273
00:23:03,247 --> 00:23:04,760
Gyu Seo, you're here?

274
00:23:07,694 --> 00:23:09,874
Su Nam's still really mad, isn't she?

275
00:23:09,899 --> 00:23:13,358
She's not going to cool off anytime soon.

276
00:23:13,434 --> 00:23:15,099
This must be really hard for you.

277
00:23:17,018 --> 00:23:20,873
- Haven't seen Gyu Yeong yet, have you?
- No.

278
00:23:21,007 --> 00:23:24,695
Go say hi and tell her
you're glad she's back.

279
00:23:26,741 --> 00:23:28,051
Later.

280
00:23:29,858 --> 00:23:33,451
Thank you for taking care of Gyu Yeong
all this time.

281
00:23:40,873 --> 00:23:44,316
The kids in this family
definitely have good genes.

282
00:23:44,454 --> 00:23:49,644
They're rough around the edges,
but warm and kind on the inside.

283
00:23:52,334 --> 00:23:57,363
But how did the guy who passed down
those genes turn out like that?

284
00:23:58,912 --> 00:24:00,672
It's a mystery.

285
00:24:09,947 --> 00:24:11,176
Why?

286
00:24:12,576 --> 00:24:16,191
Why have you been grinning
like you've lost your mind?

287
00:24:16,267 --> 00:24:17,556
- Me?
- Yeah.

288
00:24:18,981 --> 00:24:20,886
Something good happened, didn't it?

289
00:24:23,888 --> 00:24:27,604
Actually, I met my grandson.

290
00:24:29,320 --> 00:24:31,461
And he's really shaking up my heart.

291
00:24:31,486 --> 00:24:34,302
He's nothing like my son was at that age.

292
00:24:34,561 --> 00:24:36,981
His mom raised him so well.

293
00:24:37,287 --> 00:24:38,578
Fifty dollars.

294
00:24:39,118 --> 00:24:41,991
If you want to brag about your grandson,
pay 50 dollars first.

295
00:24:42,767 --> 00:24:44,044
Fine.

296
00:24:45,311 --> 00:24:46,591
Just you wait.

297
00:24:47,427 --> 00:24:51,075
Someday he won't just shake up my heart.
He'll shake up the whole world.

298
00:25:00,099 --> 00:25:01,099
Same here.

299
00:25:03,633 --> 00:25:08,613
Hey, should we take your grandson
and mine to an amusement park sometime?

300
00:25:08,847 --> 00:25:09,847
Sure.

301
00:25:12,006 --> 00:25:16,449
But grandkids aside,
let's talk about us today.

302
00:25:20,547 --> 00:25:22,158
What's going to happen to us?

303
00:25:23,486 --> 00:25:27,932
We don't have much time left,
so are we just going to keep flirting?

304
00:25:28,246 --> 00:25:29,705
Keep it platonic forever?

305
00:25:31,833 --> 00:25:33,726
Before we get any more attached,

306
00:25:35,541 --> 00:25:37,585
why don't we just stop seeing each other?

307
00:25:39,734 --> 00:25:41,468
Are you serious?

308
00:25:41,833 --> 00:25:43,703
Why would you say that?

309
00:25:43,827 --> 00:25:45,455
Before we get hurt any more.

310
00:25:46,641 --> 00:25:50,301
I'm old now. If I fall,
I won't get back up.

311
00:25:55,306 --> 00:25:57,661
What happens if we take things further?

312
00:26:00,540 --> 00:26:04,967
We haven't even held hands or hugged yet.

313
00:26:08,141 --> 00:26:10,047
I told you, holding hands is fine.

314
00:26:12,272 --> 00:26:13,959
Then what? Move in together?

315
00:26:17,861 --> 00:26:20,489
Right. That's not it either, is it?

316
00:26:22,012 --> 00:26:23,012
Right.

317
00:26:24,120 --> 00:26:27,837
If we moved in together,
the kids would say we're too old for this.

318
00:26:30,007 --> 00:26:32,614
They wouldn't treat me like their dad.
They'd probably kick me out.

319
00:26:33,660 --> 00:26:36,039
Is it their life? It's our life.

320
00:26:36,360 --> 00:26:38,123
We're still sharp.

321
00:26:38,166 --> 00:26:40,340
We're not dead yet. What's with you?

322
00:26:40,563 --> 00:26:44,540
You'd really want to live with me?

323
00:26:49,680 --> 00:26:51,101
But...

324
00:26:53,067 --> 00:26:56,986
Before that, I have a confession to make,
and I need some time.

325
00:26:58,587 --> 00:27:01,627
Actually, I have something
to confess to you too.

326
00:27:03,580 --> 00:27:04,580
Okay.

327
00:27:05,745 --> 00:27:11,053
Then next time we meet,
let's start with our confessions.

328
00:27:11,660 --> 00:27:14,905
How I lied to you, and how you lied to me.

329
00:27:17,526 --> 00:27:21,294
You're not flat broke, are you?

330
00:27:24,080 --> 00:27:25,764
Thank you. Have a nice day.

331
00:27:32,466 --> 00:27:34,566
- Excuse me.
- Yes, how can I help you?

332
00:27:38,061 --> 00:27:40,606
I'm shopping for my dad's birthday,

333
00:27:40,608 --> 00:27:42,747
so what's popular these days?

334
00:27:42,819 --> 00:27:44,443
Popular items?

335
00:27:48,360 --> 00:27:50,250
This jacket's a bestseller,

336
00:27:51,619 --> 00:27:53,551
and this one gets great reviews too.

337
00:27:54,613 --> 00:27:57,692
- Do you have a girlfriend, by any chance?
- Sorry?

338
00:27:58,661 --> 00:28:01,631
My friend fell for you at first sight.

339
00:28:02,014 --> 00:28:04,936
She's really picky,
and her standards are super high...

340
00:28:04,961 --> 00:28:08,239
Sorry. I'm already married.

341
00:28:10,787 --> 00:28:13,216
Already? How old are you?

342
00:28:13,241 --> 00:28:16,101
I married young.
I already have three kids.

343
00:28:17,193 --> 00:28:18,972
Congratulations.

344
00:28:19,187 --> 00:28:21,923
- Take your time looking around.
- Thank you.

345
00:28:22,420 --> 00:28:23,864
Welcome.

346
00:28:24,787 --> 00:28:27,507
(Seo Min Ju)

347
00:28:29,480 --> 00:28:33,066
It seems to be psychogenic aphasia
caused by stress.

348
00:28:33,193 --> 00:28:35,614
For now, take the medication
I'm prescribing,

349
00:28:35,666 --> 00:28:39,382
and come in right away
if your symptoms change.

350
00:28:39,931 --> 00:28:42,774
(Mom)

351
00:28:57,913 --> 00:28:59,502
I won't let you take Gyeol.

352
00:29:03,848 --> 00:29:05,750
Where were you all this time?

353
00:29:08,273 --> 00:29:10,342
And now you just show up out of nowhere?

354
00:29:11,487 --> 00:29:13,132
Is Gyeol some kind of object?

355
00:29:13,661 --> 00:29:15,773
Something you have to hand back
just because someone asks for it?

356
00:29:25,527 --> 00:29:29,303
I worked on an oil rig
in the North Sea off Norway.

357
00:29:30,066 --> 00:29:34,544
Hye Jeong called and told me
Jeong Hyeon was born,

358
00:29:35,131 --> 00:29:36,564
and I saw photos too.

359
00:29:38,361 --> 00:29:39,361
But...

360
00:29:41,280 --> 00:29:43,152
there was a major accident that day.

361
00:29:48,094 --> 00:29:50,841
I spent over three years in the hospital,
hovering between life and death,

362
00:29:51,935 --> 00:29:54,977
and miraculously, I survived.
So I could see my son.

363
00:29:59,701 --> 00:30:02,254
Hye Jeong left Jeong Hyeon with Gyu Rim,

364
00:30:05,127 --> 00:30:08,972
and went to the US with another man.
I found that out two years ago.

365
00:30:10,235 --> 00:30:11,720
I can't.

366
00:30:12,234 --> 00:30:15,432
I really can't do this. This isn't right.

367
00:30:15,464 --> 00:30:20,161
But Da Som's mom and U Ram's mom
both did it.

368
00:30:21,747 --> 00:30:24,220
Still, this isn't right,
don't you think, Gyeol?

369
00:30:25,194 --> 00:30:26,642
It's Gyeol's school homework.

370
00:30:26,913 --> 00:30:28,406
Just close your eyes and do it once.

371
00:30:29,933 --> 00:30:31,471
Do you have any idea...

372
00:30:33,267 --> 00:30:35,399
what Gyeol means to Gyu Rim?

373
00:30:39,427 --> 00:30:40,427
Okay.

374
00:30:41,665 --> 00:30:44,012
Okay. Let's start, Gyu Seo.

375
00:30:45,474 --> 00:30:47,385
<i>Hi friends my name is Gyeol</i>

376
00:30:47,387 --> 00:30:49,567
<i>The coolest kid in town that's me</i>

377
00:30:49,592 --> 00:30:53,440
She endured people's judgment
and prejudice,

378
00:30:54,701 --> 00:30:57,297
and gave up her own life and future...

379
00:31:00,153 --> 00:31:02,423
to protect and raise Gyeol.

380
00:31:03,424 --> 00:31:05,006
Can you even imagine that?

381
00:31:08,880 --> 00:31:09,880
I'm...

382
00:31:11,889 --> 00:31:13,061
an orphan.

383
00:31:14,839 --> 00:31:17,578
Jeong Hyeon is the only blood family
I have in this world.

384
00:31:19,740 --> 00:31:23,922
If Gyu Rim refuses,
I'll even sue if I have to.

385
00:31:25,694 --> 00:31:26,694
What?

386
00:31:27,173 --> 00:31:29,692
Honestly, wouldn't this be better
for you, Mr. Kim?

387
00:31:30,640 --> 00:31:33,858
Wouldn't it be better if you two married
and had a child of your own?

388
00:31:33,886 --> 00:31:36,330
Better? What's better about that?

389
00:31:36,378 --> 00:31:37,810
Better for whom?

390
00:31:38,366 --> 00:31:39,932
Did you ask Gyu Rim?

391
00:31:40,080 --> 00:31:41,547
Did you ask Gyeol?

392
00:31:41,930 --> 00:31:45,661
Or did you ask me?

393
00:31:45,778 --> 00:31:46,953
Mr. Kim.

394
00:31:47,920 --> 00:31:49,862
Fine. Let's go to court.

395
00:31:51,813 --> 00:31:55,088
I don't know what gives you the right
to show up like this,

396
00:31:56,138 --> 00:31:58,866
demanding Gyeol, who means
more than life to his mom,

397
00:31:58,891 --> 00:32:00,719
and being so unreasonable.

398
00:32:01,839 --> 00:32:04,195
Fine. I'll put everything on the line...

399
00:32:05,451 --> 00:32:08,330
to fight your so-called blood ties.

400
00:32:09,222 --> 00:32:10,776
So let's go to court.

401
00:32:13,120 --> 00:32:15,335
Blood tie? Give me a break.

402
00:32:16,171 --> 00:32:20,491
What's worth more
than blood in this world,

403
00:32:21,832 --> 00:32:23,830
what helps a child grow,

404
00:32:25,140 --> 00:32:27,123
what people live for,

405
00:32:28,350 --> 00:32:30,368
I'll show you all of it, loud and clear,

406
00:32:31,982 --> 00:32:33,433
so let's go to court.

407
00:32:36,880 --> 00:32:39,743
Mu Jin gave me this to make for you.

408
00:32:43,212 --> 00:32:46,318
- Gyu Min.
- Thank you.

409
00:32:46,343 --> 00:32:47,755
- Careful, it's hot.
- Okay.

410
00:32:55,747 --> 00:32:58,042
The chamomile smells so good, Gyu Rim.

411
00:32:59,833 --> 00:33:04,868
Me, Gyu Min, Gyu Seo, all of us,

412
00:33:06,007 --> 00:33:07,742
what if we became a river?

413
00:33:11,548 --> 00:33:14,451
Gyeol, what's wrong? Did you wake up?
Want me to get you some water?

414
00:33:14,783 --> 00:33:18,254
I can do it myself, so keep talking, Mom.

415
00:33:19,960 --> 00:33:21,337
Thank you.

416
00:33:24,520 --> 00:33:27,064
Here's something I read somewhere.

417
00:33:28,233 --> 00:33:33,065
A spoonful of salt in this teacup
would make the water terribly salty,

418
00:33:33,144 --> 00:33:35,778
but the river wouldn't taste salty at all.

419
00:33:39,107 --> 00:33:40,840
I know what you mean.

420
00:33:42,606 --> 00:33:45,539
Don't be a tiny teacup like this.

421
00:33:45,808 --> 00:33:47,532
Be a big, wide river. That's it, right?

422
00:33:48,050 --> 00:33:51,677
A spoonful of salt? Who cares?
Just brush it off.

423
00:33:51,860 --> 00:33:54,798
Don't be petty or narrow-minded.

424
00:33:54,926 --> 00:33:55,926
Right.

425
00:33:57,568 --> 00:34:01,531
Whether someone pours in sugar
or fish sauce,

426
00:34:01,719 --> 00:34:04,047
don't be shaken, and don't get hurt.

427
00:34:05,144 --> 00:34:07,162
Let's all live like a river.

428
00:34:19,173 --> 00:34:21,849
- Gyeol.
- Mu Jin.

429
00:34:22,871 --> 00:34:24,640
What brings you here so early?

430
00:34:24,879 --> 00:34:28,211
- Did you come to see Mom?
- No, I came to see you.

431
00:34:29,787 --> 00:34:32,329
I even baked meringues for you last night.

432
00:34:32,354 --> 00:34:34,734
Share them with your friends.

433
00:34:36,574 --> 00:34:38,159
Thank you.

434
00:34:40,053 --> 00:34:41,265
Come here for a sec.

435
00:34:42,809 --> 00:34:45,675
Instead of going to school today,

436
00:34:46,904 --> 00:34:48,308
want to skip with me?

437
00:34:48,867 --> 00:34:53,086
Should we go back to that river
and skip stones?

438
00:34:54,481 --> 00:34:56,089
Don't you have work?

439
00:34:56,994 --> 00:34:58,274
I can skip work too.

440
00:34:58,396 --> 00:34:59,842
Don't tempt me.

441
00:35:00,322 --> 00:35:03,031
Adults shouldn't do that to kids.

442
00:35:03,803 --> 00:35:05,520
I'm off to school.

443
00:35:08,027 --> 00:35:10,491
Gyeol, let's go together.
I'll walk you there today.

444
00:35:17,366 --> 00:35:19,670
Can't we just let go and walk?

445
00:35:19,794 --> 00:35:20,794
Why?

446
00:35:21,191 --> 00:35:22,937
If the kids see us,

447
00:35:22,965 --> 00:35:25,619
they might think it's weird.

448
00:35:25,644 --> 00:35:26,936
What's weird about it?

449
00:35:27,973 --> 00:35:32,794
Kids who don't know us
might think you're my dad.

450
00:35:33,862 --> 00:35:35,705
I'm as good as your dad.

451
00:35:35,844 --> 00:35:37,645
I'm going to marry your mom soon.

452
00:35:38,323 --> 00:35:40,163
I even got permission from my mom.

453
00:35:41,767 --> 00:35:42,767
Really?

454
00:35:43,141 --> 00:35:46,211
Yes. I'll be your dad soon.

455
00:35:46,236 --> 00:35:49,154
If your friends ask,
proudly tell them I'm your dad.

456
00:35:50,381 --> 00:35:54,187
But you're not married yet.

457
00:35:55,240 --> 00:35:58,597
So you won't hold hands because
your friends might get the wrong idea?

458
00:36:00,278 --> 00:36:01,900
That stings.

459
00:36:02,753 --> 00:36:04,696
Gyeol, I'm hurt,

460
00:36:04,884 --> 00:36:06,454
and I'm about to sulk. Big time.

461
00:36:07,046 --> 00:36:08,877
Then we can hold hands.

462
00:36:09,281 --> 00:36:10,848
If the kids ask,

463
00:36:11,036 --> 00:36:14,386
I'll tell them, "He's going to be my dad."

464
00:36:14,506 --> 00:36:17,285
- Is that okay?
- Thanks, Gyeol.

465
00:36:18,779 --> 00:36:22,326
I'll be a really good dad to you.

466
00:36:24,660 --> 00:36:28,251
I hope you become a river too, Mu Jin.

467
00:36:29,754 --> 00:36:30,754
Let's go.

468
00:36:32,960 --> 00:36:34,753
What do you mean, become a river?

469
00:36:36,000 --> 00:36:38,254
Are you saying I'm narrow-minded?

470
00:36:38,313 --> 00:36:40,783
No. Come on, let's go.

471
00:36:41,441 --> 00:36:43,314
You just dissed me, didn't you?

472
00:36:43,315 --> 00:36:46,393
No. I'll explain everything later,
so let's just go.

473
00:36:55,349 --> 00:36:59,327
Hey. When are you going home?

474
00:36:59,727 --> 00:37:01,047
I'm not sure myself.

475
00:37:01,072 --> 00:37:02,947
If you don't know, who does?

476
00:37:05,101 --> 00:37:08,616
- Is it that bad sleeping next to me?
- Yeah.

477
00:37:08,839 --> 00:37:12,081
How can you snore that loudly?

478
00:37:12,314 --> 00:37:13,991
I thought it was thunder.

479
00:37:14,016 --> 00:37:16,552
You're no better, Mr. Han.

480
00:37:16,747 --> 00:37:19,847
Your snoring nearly made me go home,

481
00:37:20,088 --> 00:37:22,056
but I put up with it, you know.

482
00:37:22,081 --> 00:37:26,253
Hey. Don't put up with it. Go home.
I won't stop you.

483
00:37:26,627 --> 00:37:29,016
Don't give Heung Sik a hard time.

484
00:37:29,393 --> 00:37:31,522
He got kicked out because of Gyu Yeong.

485
00:37:31,946 --> 00:37:33,950
Heung Sik, make yourself at home.

486
00:37:35,760 --> 00:37:36,760
Did you hear that?

487
00:37:44,961 --> 00:37:46,425
Forget the company, forget everything.

488
00:37:46,427 --> 00:37:47,874
I might as well die.

489
00:37:50,280 --> 00:37:52,514
I was only acting tough
in front of Chairman Jang.

490
00:37:52,660 --> 00:37:54,532
I was so angry and bitter.

491
00:37:56,478 --> 00:37:59,944
Forget it. My life is beyond saving,

492
00:38:00,031 --> 00:38:02,388
and I've got a one-way ticket
to rock bottom.

493
00:38:04,080 --> 00:38:06,534
I'm too ashamed to show my face.

494
00:38:06,846 --> 00:38:10,720
People will laugh at me,
look down on me, and point fingers.

495
00:38:13,643 --> 00:38:16,142
I don't know. I can't go on. No, I won't.

496
00:38:16,260 --> 00:38:18,460
I'd rather die than live like this.

497
00:38:23,040 --> 00:38:24,598
Don't you know how to knock?

498
00:38:25,008 --> 00:38:27,160
Now that I've hit rock bottom,
you're looking down on me too?

499
00:38:28,994 --> 00:38:31,093
Hey, Han Gyu Rim's here. Call me later.

500
00:38:38,841 --> 00:38:39,841
Die, then.

501
00:38:40,977 --> 00:38:43,370
- What?
- I said die.

502
00:38:43,894 --> 00:38:45,651
If you want to die,
then die. What else can you do?

503
00:38:46,187 --> 00:38:48,139
I'll give you a proper funeral.

504
00:38:49,394 --> 00:38:52,480
If you're going to die over something
this small, you might as well do it now.

505
00:38:52,821 --> 00:38:55,668
With a mindset that weak,
you're just a waste of food anyway.

506
00:38:55,787 --> 00:38:57,937
You're asking for it!

507
00:39:00,580 --> 00:39:02,969
I'm not dying. Why would I die?

508
00:39:03,287 --> 00:39:06,241
With my siblings, my Gyeol,
and Mu Jin still here,

509
00:39:06,330 --> 00:39:08,113
I'd be too worried and bitter to die.

510
00:39:12,812 --> 00:39:16,306
Get out. I don't even have the energy
to fight with you right now.

511
00:39:20,047 --> 00:39:21,772
Just let it go, Gyu Yeong.

512
00:39:24,574 --> 00:39:25,801
What?

513
00:39:26,628 --> 00:39:27,628
That.

514
00:39:28,725 --> 00:39:30,337
That thing you're holding on to,

515
00:39:31,628 --> 00:39:32,906
just let it go.

516
00:39:33,280 --> 00:39:35,047
What am I holding on to?

517
00:39:35,254 --> 00:39:37,549
I've lost everything.
I don't have a penny.

518
00:39:49,974 --> 00:39:51,201
What do you think you're doing?

519
00:39:51,441 --> 00:39:53,414
Let go of me. Let go!

520
00:39:54,143 --> 00:39:55,427
I can't let you go either.

521
00:39:56,513 --> 00:39:57,754
No, I won't.

522
00:39:58,086 --> 00:40:02,494
No matter what happens,
I'm never letting you go again.

523
00:40:04,592 --> 00:40:06,173
Are you pitying me?

524
00:40:06,829 --> 00:40:10,817
You know how much I hate cheap pity
like that,

525
00:40:10,842 --> 00:40:12,620
so do you want to die or something?

526
00:40:12,653 --> 00:40:14,515
It must've been so hard.

527
00:40:16,640 --> 00:40:20,292
You must've been so lonely
all by yourself, Gyu Yeong.

528
00:40:22,767 --> 00:40:24,715
What are you talking about?

529
00:40:25,026 --> 00:40:28,116
Let go of me, Han Gyu Rim!

530
00:40:29,288 --> 00:40:31,324
I'm never leaving you alone again.

531
00:40:32,340 --> 00:40:34,829
No matter how much you push me away
or kick me,

532
00:40:35,040 --> 00:40:38,276
I'll meddle in every part of your life
and nag you nonstop.

533
00:40:38,760 --> 00:40:41,627
And that worthless pride
you're clinging to,

534
00:40:41,652 --> 00:40:43,297
I'll smash it to pieces.

535
00:40:44,254 --> 00:40:46,140
If you go down the wrong path again,

536
00:40:46,800 --> 00:40:49,034
I'll break your legs if I have to,

537
00:40:49,323 --> 00:40:50,795
but I won't let you go.

538
00:40:52,785 --> 00:40:55,828
Who do you think you are?

539
00:40:56,013 --> 00:40:58,907
Who are you to care how a stranger lives?

540
00:40:59,873 --> 00:41:02,634
Why would you be a stranger?

541
00:41:02,973 --> 00:41:05,427
How are we strangers, Gyu Yeong?

542
00:41:06,387 --> 00:41:08,506
I'm your family. I'm your sister.

543
00:41:09,793 --> 00:41:11,926
I'm Han Gyu Rim,
Han Gyu Yeong's older sister.

544
00:41:21,427 --> 00:41:23,530
Who do you think you are?

545
00:41:38,259 --> 00:41:40,532
What's going on?

546
00:41:40,580 --> 00:41:42,952
Is Gyu Rim hitting Gyu Yeong?

547
00:41:43,393 --> 00:41:45,442
If she's asking for it, she gets hit.

548
00:41:46,547 --> 00:41:48,614
Even if she's your least favorite kid,

549
00:41:49,010 --> 00:41:51,378
aren't you a little too obvious
about disliking Gyu Yeong?

550
00:41:52,687 --> 00:41:54,866
Are you taking Gyu Yeong's side now?

551
00:41:55,044 --> 00:41:57,661
Did you two get close or something?

552
00:41:58,605 --> 00:42:00,974
No. Absolutely not. No way.

553
00:42:01,420 --> 00:42:03,707
Why deny it three times?

554
00:42:03,879 --> 00:42:06,368
That's starting to bother me.

555
00:42:09,740 --> 00:42:11,030
Look who's here.

556
00:42:11,434 --> 00:42:12,894
Mu Jin's here.

557
00:42:13,261 --> 00:42:14,714
Hello, I'm Kim Mu Jin.

558
00:42:14,781 --> 00:42:17,657
I know you. I'm Heung Sik.

559
00:42:31,194 --> 00:42:34,983
Gyu Rim. Mu Jin's here.

560
00:42:38,954 --> 00:42:40,466
Is Gyu Yeong okay?

561
00:42:45,555 --> 00:42:50,058
Son-in-law Kim! It's been ages!

562
00:42:50,083 --> 00:42:54,344
This poop-brown suede looks so stylish.

563
00:42:55,301 --> 00:42:57,448
I'm sorry I haven't visited more often.

564
00:42:58,318 --> 00:42:59,560
Sorry? That'll be 50 cents.

565
00:43:01,720 --> 00:43:03,652
What brings you here this early?

566
00:43:06,399 --> 00:43:07,999
I was passing by and got hungry.

567
00:43:08,060 --> 00:43:09,440
Good timing, Mu Jin.

568
00:43:10,240 --> 00:43:14,387
Mr. Han and I were just eating bibimbap
out of a big bowl, and it's to die for.

569
00:43:15,041 --> 00:43:17,815
You didn't come because you missed me,
but because you were hungry?

570
00:43:18,768 --> 00:43:20,965
If he missed anyone, it's Gyu Rim.

571
00:43:20,990 --> 00:43:23,025
Why would he miss you, Mr. Han?

572
00:43:23,700 --> 00:43:26,012
No, sir. I was hungry,

573
00:43:26,621 --> 00:43:28,537
but I also wanted to see you.

574
00:43:29,159 --> 00:43:30,846
Right?

575
00:43:31,254 --> 00:43:33,112
You be quiet.

576
00:43:33,921 --> 00:43:36,557
I was just eating, but since you're here,

577
00:43:36,838 --> 00:43:40,821
why don't we eat together
and hang out afterward?

578
00:43:40,846 --> 00:43:42,774
Come here, son-in-law Kim.

579
00:43:43,089 --> 00:43:44,402
Let's go.

580
00:43:47,600 --> 00:43:49,742
The real villain's right here.

581
00:43:49,766 --> 00:43:53,033
Mr. Han must've lost all his tact
in this summer's heat.

582
00:43:56,229 --> 00:43:59,127
You didn't hit Gyu Yeong, did you?

583
00:44:10,531 --> 00:44:12,897
(Mu Jin's Mother)

584
00:44:28,260 --> 00:44:30,455
For a rich heir,
you're awfully down-to-earth.

585
00:44:34,456 --> 00:44:35,780
He's from a rich family?

586
00:44:36,347 --> 00:44:39,890
No, he's just an ordinary guy.

587
00:44:47,826 --> 00:44:49,134
I'm done eating.

588
00:44:50,160 --> 00:44:52,298
- May I go see Gyu Rim now?
- Upstairs.

589
00:44:54,267 --> 00:44:56,483
I can't wait another second to see her.

590
00:44:56,637 --> 00:44:57,637
Thanks for the meal.

591
00:44:58,800 --> 00:45:00,618
- I'll leave this here.
- Okay.

592
00:45:04,681 --> 00:45:06,164
What's with him?

593
00:45:06,374 --> 00:45:08,054
I thought he came to see me.

594
00:45:11,813 --> 00:45:14,073
This is Mu Jin's mom.

595
00:45:15,219 --> 00:45:19,134
If you have time,
could we meet briefly today?

596
00:45:19,699 --> 00:45:21,592
Without telling Mu Jin.

597
00:45:25,713 --> 00:45:27,053
(Mu Jin)

598
00:45:31,360 --> 00:45:32,710
Hey, Mu Jin.

599
00:45:32,967 --> 00:45:34,283
Which room is yours?

600
00:45:34,440 --> 00:45:38,036
Judging by Gyeol's sticker here,
is it this one?

601
00:45:51,015 --> 00:45:52,201
Can I come in?

602
00:45:53,460 --> 00:45:55,307
Yeah. Come in.

603
00:46:08,554 --> 00:46:11,711
So this is the room you and Gyeol share.

604
00:46:12,574 --> 00:46:16,183
It's much nicer than I imagined.

605
00:46:18,334 --> 00:46:20,811
- Can I sit?
- Sure, sit down.

606
00:46:23,673 --> 00:46:24,965
That.

607
00:46:43,027 --> 00:46:45,134
Are your injuries any better?

608
00:46:45,860 --> 00:46:48,624
Yeah. All healed. I'm fine now.

609
00:46:54,080 --> 00:46:55,210
Hey...

610
00:46:58,213 --> 00:46:59,519
Want to go to the States with me?

611
00:47:01,307 --> 00:47:02,314
What?

612
00:47:05,393 --> 00:47:08,416
I have a friend who runs
a restaurant in Boston.

613
00:47:08,773 --> 00:47:11,513
He's been begging me to work with him
for years.

614
00:47:12,753 --> 00:47:14,413
Let's go to the States with Gyeol,
just the three of us.

615
00:47:15,421 --> 00:47:19,143
We can show Gyeol a bigger world,

616
00:47:20,257 --> 00:47:22,699
and he'll even set us up with a house.

617
00:47:24,846 --> 00:47:27,753
All of a sudden? Out of nowhere?

618
00:47:29,628 --> 00:47:31,975
I know it's sudden and out of nowhere,

619
00:47:33,428 --> 00:47:36,560
but if it bothers you to go alone,
we can bring the whole family.

620
00:47:40,120 --> 00:47:42,685
No, wait. Not the States.

621
00:47:44,700 --> 00:47:46,400
Let's go to the farthest place from Korea.

622
00:47:46,713 --> 00:47:48,497
Somewhere no one can find us.

623
00:47:48,624 --> 00:47:50,906
Somewhere that's not even on a map.

624
00:47:52,740 --> 00:47:54,146
Did something happen?

625
00:47:57,047 --> 00:47:59,024
No, nothing.

626
00:47:59,708 --> 00:48:03,605
I'm just a little tired
of dealing with people,

627
00:48:04,599 --> 00:48:08,540
so I thought, what if the three of us
lived somewhere with no one around?

628
00:48:12,627 --> 00:48:13,840
Let's move abroad.

629
00:48:18,361 --> 00:48:19,793
(Kitchen, Bath, Home and Living)

630
00:48:19,818 --> 00:48:21,082
(Younglim Industrial Co., Ltd.)

631
00:48:21,107 --> 00:48:22,580
Welcome.

632
00:48:28,580 --> 00:48:29,859
Ms. Han Gyu Rim.

633
00:48:34,527 --> 00:48:36,834
Come on, Mom's over there.

634
00:48:46,167 --> 00:48:48,631
A friend of mine uses your products,

635
00:48:48,656 --> 00:48:51,122
and he says he doesn't even feel
the cold in winter.

636
00:48:51,293 --> 00:48:53,426
- You know Chairman Park in Yuseong?
- Yes.

637
00:48:53,901 --> 00:48:56,994
He's really sensitive to cold
and very particular,

638
00:48:57,019 --> 00:48:59,085
and he highly recommended you.

639
00:48:59,367 --> 00:49:02,694
Yes, we paid special attention
to insulation.

640
00:49:02,719 --> 00:49:06,212
Once you try it, you'll see
what a great product it is.

641
00:49:06,833 --> 00:49:11,065
With a frame this slim,
it feels different.

642
00:49:11,933 --> 00:49:14,562
You have a remarkable eye, ma'am.

643
00:49:16,273 --> 00:49:19,116
- Ma'am.
- Yes.

644
00:49:30,833 --> 00:49:32,792
It's been a while.

645
00:49:33,894 --> 00:49:34,910
Yes.

646
00:49:36,170 --> 00:49:39,046
I'd like to talk with the person
who'll actually be using it.

647
00:49:39,233 --> 00:49:42,407
Of course. Please take your time
and call me if you need anything.

648
00:49:46,586 --> 00:49:49,227
Then I'll go look around over there too.

649
00:49:51,874 --> 00:49:53,500
You don't have to be so nervous.

650
00:49:53,813 --> 00:49:58,493
I don't know what my mom's seen lately,
but she's like a toothless tiger now,

651
00:49:58,518 --> 00:50:01,243
so even if she wanted to eat you alive,
she couldn't.

652
00:50:01,353 --> 00:50:02,600
Kim Yun Jin.

653
00:50:03,913 --> 00:50:04,926
Good luck.

654
00:50:16,147 --> 00:50:17,747
You've lost a little weight.

655
00:50:20,840 --> 00:50:22,353
His name's Gyeol, right?

656
00:50:23,307 --> 00:50:25,613
You did a great job raising your son.

657
00:50:27,647 --> 00:50:30,633
You met Gyeol?

658
00:50:30,768 --> 00:50:32,974
My goodness.

659
00:50:33,321 --> 00:50:36,618
I asked him to keep our meeting
a secret from his mom.

660
00:50:36,621 --> 00:50:39,067
And he really didn't tell you, did he?

661
00:50:39,193 --> 00:50:42,035
Such a little guy,
and he knows how to keep a secret.

662
00:50:42,354 --> 00:50:45,947
You raised your son
much better than I did, Gyu Rim.

663
00:50:47,953 --> 00:50:49,947
Please, there's no need to be so formal
with me.

664
00:50:52,367 --> 00:50:55,408
All right, let's drop the formalities.

665
00:50:55,433 --> 00:50:57,272
We'll be family soon.

666
00:50:59,013 --> 00:51:02,513
While we're at it, I'd like you two
to get married soon.

667
00:51:02,613 --> 00:51:06,292
For Gyeol's sake too,
before the year is out.

668
00:51:07,319 --> 00:51:09,895
Whether you have a small wedding,
the kind that's trendy these days,

669
00:51:09,920 --> 00:51:12,630
or a grand wedding
inviting everyone you know,

670
00:51:12,632 --> 00:51:14,480
it's up to you two.

671
00:51:14,514 --> 00:51:18,440
And as for your new home,
whether it's on Earth or Mars,

672
00:51:18,609 --> 00:51:21,917
live wherever you want,
as long as you're not afraid of heights.

673
00:51:23,805 --> 00:51:26,146
You don't need to exchange
any wedding gifts.

674
00:51:26,195 --> 00:51:29,746
And as for wedding rings,
copper or diamond,

675
00:51:29,771 --> 00:51:31,594
get whatever you can afford.

676
00:51:31,619 --> 00:51:33,139
What else is there?

677
00:51:33,214 --> 00:51:36,152
Anyway, it's not my life.

678
00:51:36,187 --> 00:51:38,830
It's yours, Kim Mu Jin and Han Gyu Rim,

679
00:51:39,077 --> 00:51:41,307
so live however you two want.

680
00:51:44,474 --> 00:51:48,544
Still, as your mother-in-law,
I'd like to give you one gift.

681
00:51:48,986 --> 00:51:51,739
Let me redo the interior of your home...

682
00:51:51,764 --> 00:51:55,011
however you like. Don't say no.

683
00:51:59,434 --> 00:52:00,608
You...

684
00:52:02,916 --> 00:52:05,480
You must've had a hard time
raising a child alone.

685
00:52:06,387 --> 00:52:10,805
But you raised Gyeol to be such a good,
wonderful kid,

686
00:52:11,706 --> 00:52:14,904
so this is my way of rewarding you.

687
00:52:18,187 --> 00:52:19,973
When I see how you raised your child,

688
00:52:21,284 --> 00:52:23,400
I can see what kind of person you are.

689
00:52:24,360 --> 00:52:27,946
I think I finally understand...

690
00:52:30,734 --> 00:52:33,107
why Mu Jin could never forget you
or let you go.

691
00:52:45,814 --> 00:52:47,821
Please forget everything that happened.

692
00:52:48,238 --> 00:52:52,278
I know it won't be easy, but please,
for Mu Jin's sake.

693
00:52:59,807 --> 00:53:01,654
I'm sorry, Gyu Rim.

694
00:53:22,033 --> 00:53:23,047
Well?

695
00:53:26,340 --> 00:53:28,504
- What did they say?
- First, sit down.

696
00:53:32,976 --> 00:53:34,338
And calm down.

697
00:53:34,363 --> 00:53:36,089
Just tell me. What is it?

698
00:53:36,114 --> 00:53:37,239
What do you mean, calm down?

699
00:53:37,264 --> 00:53:39,699
If you're already getting worked up,
I won't tell you.

700
00:53:42,339 --> 00:53:46,966
Okay. I won't get worked up. Tell me.

701
00:53:50,721 --> 00:53:52,142
It doesn't look like Gyu Rim...

702
00:53:53,536 --> 00:53:57,934
formally adopted Gyeol
through the proper legal process.

703
00:54:01,800 --> 00:54:05,733
If Gyeol's biological father sues
and it goes to trial,

704
00:54:07,646 --> 00:54:09,106
I don't know what'll happen.

705
00:54:09,707 --> 00:54:13,154
That's so irresponsible.
How can you not know?

706
00:54:13,320 --> 00:54:15,293
You're a lawyer and you don't know that?

707
00:54:15,407 --> 00:54:17,076
How are you even a lawyer?

708
00:54:17,101 --> 00:54:20,554
I'm not a lawyer anymore! I quit
to work for you, remember?

709
00:54:23,620 --> 00:54:26,920
Why is there never a quiet moment
in Gyu Rim's life?

710
00:54:27,094 --> 00:54:29,567
She's had more trouble than anyone
I've ever known.

711
00:54:29,592 --> 00:54:31,701
Forget it. I'll block it all.

712
00:54:31,726 --> 00:54:33,557
Let any storm come Gyu Rim's way.

713
00:54:33,582 --> 00:54:34,921
I'll block every one of them.

714
00:54:34,946 --> 00:54:37,295
If they sold shields
like Captain Africa's,

715
00:54:38,386 --> 00:54:40,874
I'd buy one for you. Seriously.

716
00:54:46,313 --> 00:54:50,227
Wait, I was supposed to go
somewhere today.

717
00:54:51,127 --> 00:54:54,087
It was really important. What was it?

718
00:54:57,607 --> 00:55:00,014
This isn't me looking at you
like you're pathetic.

719
00:55:00,021 --> 00:55:04,181
This is me feeling really sorry for you.

720
00:55:05,960 --> 00:55:07,542
Right!

721
00:55:11,493 --> 00:55:14,099
I'd marry any guy right now.

722
00:55:15,434 --> 00:55:17,734
Mu Jin loves this brand.

723
00:55:20,534 --> 00:55:21,920
What do you think, Gyu Rim?

724
00:55:23,540 --> 00:55:25,100
They're beautiful.

725
00:55:31,434 --> 00:55:33,480
My mom caught you off guard, didn't she?

726
00:55:35,707 --> 00:55:40,530
Once she changes her mind,
she becomes a whole new person,

727
00:55:40,832 --> 00:55:43,726
and floors it wherever she wants to go.

728
00:55:44,126 --> 00:55:46,766
Where do you think Mu Jin gets
his full-throttle drive from?

729
00:55:48,873 --> 00:55:49,906
Gyu Rim.

730
00:55:53,514 --> 00:55:54,760
Mu Jin.

731
00:55:55,884 --> 00:55:58,504
Mom had something to tell Gyu Rim alone,

732
00:55:58,529 --> 00:56:02,807
so she scheduled you two 30 minutes apart,
but you showed up an hour late.

733
00:56:02,832 --> 00:56:05,038
Mom had to leave for an executive meeting.

734
00:56:05,063 --> 00:56:07,562
She said she told Gyu Rim
everything herself.

735
00:56:08,600 --> 00:56:12,100
What did she tell you? What did Mom say?

736
00:56:13,707 --> 00:56:15,193
I'll get going, then.

737
00:56:17,693 --> 00:56:21,473
These are going in your home,
so pick them out yourselves.

738
00:56:29,391 --> 00:56:32,057
I never formally apologized to you, did I?

739
00:56:33,530 --> 00:56:35,233
I'll apologize properly now.

740
00:56:35,574 --> 00:56:37,273
I'm sorry for everything.

741
00:56:37,907 --> 00:56:40,873
Next time, let's meet on happier terms.

742
00:56:43,307 --> 00:56:44,313
Bye.

743
00:56:49,693 --> 00:56:50,720
Are you okay?

744
00:56:52,381 --> 00:56:53,414
No.

745
00:56:54,047 --> 00:56:55,614
What did my mom say?

746
00:56:55,787 --> 00:56:57,314
Did she say something to you again?

747
00:56:58,247 --> 00:56:59,306
No.

748
00:57:01,174 --> 00:57:05,714
She wants to give us an interior makeover
here as a wedding gift,

749
00:57:06,974 --> 00:57:10,207
and she really hopes I won't refuse.

750
00:57:13,507 --> 00:57:14,820
A wedding gift?

751
00:57:15,274 --> 00:57:17,687
She was so warm and kind.

752
00:57:18,767 --> 00:57:20,480
For Gyeol's sake,

753
00:57:21,574 --> 00:57:23,993
she'd like us to get married
within the year.

754
00:57:28,519 --> 00:57:29,579
But...

755
00:57:31,780 --> 00:57:36,406
I think she believes Gyeol is your son.

756
00:57:40,381 --> 00:57:41,940
Gyeol is my son.

757
00:57:46,087 --> 00:57:47,493
Don't get confused, Han Gyu Rim.

758
00:57:47,518 --> 00:57:49,151
If he's your son, he's my son.

759
00:57:49,666 --> 00:57:51,459
No matter what anyone says, he's my son.

760
00:57:55,953 --> 00:57:59,378
Gyu Rim, are you okay?

761
00:58:05,541 --> 00:58:06,554
Welcome.

762
00:58:14,054 --> 00:58:16,174
Have you heard from Hui Na?

763
00:58:23,154 --> 00:58:27,389
She keeps ignoring my calls,
and she took sick leave from school...

764
00:58:28,674 --> 00:58:30,480
She doesn't seem to be home either,

765
00:58:31,994 --> 00:58:33,667
and I'm worried
she's done something reckless.

766
00:58:36,168 --> 00:58:37,781
Isn't this what you wanted?

767
00:58:40,000 --> 00:58:41,007
What?

768
00:58:42,567 --> 00:58:44,467
Didn't things turn out the way you wanted?

769
00:58:48,560 --> 00:58:50,796
Yeah, that's right.

770
00:58:51,544 --> 00:58:54,451
I wished you two would break up,
be miserable,

771
00:58:54,604 --> 00:58:57,060
and fall apart completely.

772
00:58:59,476 --> 00:59:01,884
This is exactly what I wanted,

773
00:59:02,985 --> 00:59:05,240
or at least, I thought it was,

774
00:59:07,880 --> 00:59:09,293
but I guess not.

775
00:59:11,961 --> 00:59:13,154
What kind of nonsense is that?

776
00:59:13,179 --> 00:59:17,927
I don't know what nonsense
I'm saying right now either,

777
00:59:18,700 --> 00:59:21,880
but I'm going crazy worrying
something's happened to Hui Na.

778
00:59:22,793 --> 00:59:25,213
I keep getting this bad feeling.

779
00:59:28,220 --> 00:59:29,411
Get lost.

780
00:59:33,561 --> 00:59:35,627
She's my only friend.

781
00:59:38,287 --> 00:59:43,049
Kwon Hui Na is the only friend I've got.

782
00:59:43,514 --> 00:59:45,673
Get lost. Now.

783
00:59:59,026 --> 01:00:01,259
(Cousin)

784
01:00:03,900 --> 01:00:06,034
Hui Na, it's Ju Yun.

785
01:00:06,260 --> 01:00:07,920
You're home, aren't you?

786
01:00:08,206 --> 01:00:12,013
Open the door. Your mom's here too.

787
01:00:12,493 --> 01:00:15,119
Your mom came up from Andong.

788
01:00:17,900 --> 01:00:19,847
Hui Na. Kwon Hui Na.

789
01:00:19,872 --> 01:00:24,343
It's Mom. Open the door. Hui Na.

790
01:00:26,146 --> 01:00:28,019
Hui Na!

791
01:00:31,034 --> 01:00:34,420
Hui Na. Kwon Hui Na. It's Mom.

792
01:00:35,920 --> 01:00:37,786
Open the door.

793
01:00:53,441 --> 01:00:55,007
Yes, Gyu O.

794
01:00:58,865 --> 01:01:02,385
Hello? This is Gyeol.

795
01:01:02,921 --> 01:01:05,060
Did you call the wrong number?

796
01:01:05,887 --> 01:01:07,240
No, Han Gyeol.

797
01:01:08,494 --> 01:01:09,713
Where are you right now?

798
01:01:09,738 --> 01:01:12,991
At Da Som's.
We're doing homework together.

799
01:01:13,761 --> 01:01:18,167
Did your homeroom teacher
not come to school today?

800
01:01:19,534 --> 01:01:22,014
How do you know that, Gyu O?

801
01:01:26,106 --> 01:01:27,446
I just happened to hear about it.

802
01:01:28,180 --> 01:01:31,593
Your teacher's friend is someone I know.

803
01:01:31,618 --> 01:01:34,058
No way. What a small world.

804
01:01:34,320 --> 01:01:38,139
Yeah, it really is a small world.

805
01:01:39,434 --> 01:01:44,601
What's wrong, Hui Na? What is it?

806
01:01:56,514 --> 01:01:58,624
You used to call several times a day,

807
01:01:58,649 --> 01:02:02,334
asking about your dad,
asking about your brother.

808
01:02:03,440 --> 01:02:06,504
But you stopped calling
and wouldn't answer,

809
01:02:06,529 --> 01:02:10,558
and only sent texts.
I knew something was off.

810
01:02:11,119 --> 01:02:13,980
I wondered if something had happened.

811
01:02:22,620 --> 01:02:28,685
What is going on?

812
01:02:29,632 --> 01:02:35,100
You were always so feisty.
Why can't you talk all of a sudden?

813
01:02:36,007 --> 01:02:38,347
What on earth hurt you so badly...

814
01:02:41,434 --> 01:02:44,904
that you're this sick at heart...

815
01:02:48,360 --> 01:02:49,931
Is it because of Han Gyu O?

816
01:02:50,586 --> 01:02:53,955
Did the shock of dumping that gigolo
do this to you?

817
01:02:56,587 --> 01:03:00,747
What? Han Gyu O? Gigolo?

818
01:03:08,373 --> 01:03:10,359
Yeah, I'm almost there.

819
01:03:12,093 --> 01:03:16,502
Tell your mom the sponge cake was so good.

820
01:03:17,996 --> 01:03:20,906
Okay. See you at school, Lee Da Som.

821
01:03:20,933 --> 01:03:22,260
Yeah, bye.

822
01:03:23,407 --> 01:03:24,433
Han Gyeol.

823
01:03:33,360 --> 01:03:34,800
Who are you?

824
01:03:35,341 --> 01:03:42,245
(Suragan Side Dishes)

825
01:03:42,706 --> 01:03:43,759
Here we are.

826
01:03:51,860 --> 01:03:53,373
Thanks, Mu Jin.

827
01:03:54,488 --> 01:03:55,507
Go on.

828
01:03:57,367 --> 01:03:59,714
I told them I might not make it in today.

829
01:04:00,361 --> 01:04:03,340
Even without me, the new sous-chef
does a great job.

830
01:04:05,533 --> 01:04:07,933
Still, go.

831
01:04:14,634 --> 01:04:16,320
You're still trembling.

832
01:04:19,767 --> 01:04:22,500
Stop shaking. It's okay.

833
01:04:23,954 --> 01:04:27,541
We're okay now, and we'll keep being okay.

834
01:04:28,140 --> 01:04:29,660
You're Gyeol's mom.

835
01:04:30,440 --> 01:04:32,567
The strongest person in the world.

836
01:04:34,247 --> 01:04:35,640
Don't be scared, Gyu Rim.

837
01:04:37,880 --> 01:04:38,913
Don't be scared.

838
01:04:40,853 --> 01:04:42,480
Mom!

839
01:04:48,067 --> 01:04:50,621
Gyeol, why are you crying? What happened?

840
01:05:30,857 --> 01:05:33,202
(Love on the Menu)

841
01:05:33,227 --> 01:05:35,273
Heung Sik,
do you happen to like Gyu Yeong?

842
01:05:35,298 --> 01:05:36,825
Do you really like Han Gyu Yeong?

843
01:05:36,850 --> 01:05:39,713
It's Mom, Gyu Yeong.
Can we meet for a bit?

844
01:05:39,738 --> 01:05:42,531
Hui Na, I'm the one who ruined us,
not you.

845
01:05:42,556 --> 01:05:44,203
Don't you recognize me, Gyu Rim?

846
01:05:44,228 --> 01:05:46,951
I saw my son for the first time
in eight years,

847
01:05:46,976 --> 01:05:49,190
and he's grown up so beautifully.

848
01:05:49,215 --> 01:05:51,335
Did Lee Hyeon Beom come to see you too?

849
01:05:51,360 --> 01:05:54,860
I'm Hong Ok Seon,
chairwoman of Dongyun Group.

850
01:05:54,901 --> 01:05:57,194
I won't let them take Gyeol.

851
01:05:57,300 --> 01:06:00,446
Having you here makes me feel
so much safer.

852
01:06:00,540 --> 01:06:02,811
No matter what happens,
nobody's taking him from me.

853
01:06:03,769 --> 01:06:05,569
Dramaday.me
